"text": "← Back to Portfolio Entertainment Creativity, performance, and presentation. With a diverse background encompassing college and community theater, musical pursuits, and online video performance, my professional endeavors benefit from a unique blend of artistic skills and multimedia expertise. Theater On stage in a college production Stage credits Riverside Shakespeare Company Romeo and Juliet , actor May – Jul 2008 A Midsummer Night's Dream , actor 2009 College productions One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest Aug – Dec 2007 Macbeth Jan – May 2008 The Holocaust Cantata Mar – Apr 2008 The Crucible Aug – Dec 2008 Much Ado About Nothing , assistant director Jan – Apr 2009 Pancakes: The Musical Sep – Dec 2010 Convicts Jan – Apr 2011 Theater is where I first learned to hold a room. From 2007 to 2011 I performed with a community Shakespeare company in Northern Michigan and in a string of college productions, everything from classic tragedy and American drama to a choral piece and something called Pancakes: The Musical . With the Riverside Shakespeare Company I acted in Romeo and Juliet and A Midsummer Night's Dream . Shakespeare is a great teacher of the basics: you can't get through those lines without breath control, clear diction, and knowing exactly what you mean by every word, and an audience lets you know right away when you don't. In college I joined the casts of One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest , Macbeth , The Crucible , The Holocaust Cantata , Pancakes: The Musical , and Convicts . Months of rehearsals taught me to memorize quickly, take notes gracefully, adjust on the fly, and trust the people around me. In 2009 I stepped to the other side of the stage as a teacher's aide and assistant director for a college play production class's Much Ado About Nothing , coaching students on memorization and acting technique and helping put together the course materials. It was one of my first tastes of teaching. The same skills (projection, pacing, reading the room, and staying calm when something goes sideways) are the ones I use in front of every training group today. Acting Directing Online video & audio Charity livestreaming: I stream gameplay to raise money for Extra Life and Children's Miracle Network Hospitals (since 2016), promoting streams on social media and building a welcoming community. Podcasting: guest on the YA!Cast young-adult book podcast (episode: Paper Towns ). Livestreaming Charity fundraising Podcasting ← Back to Portfolio Game testing Pre-release testing and bug reporting for 21 games, from MMOs to indie puzzle games (most recent first; dates are the testing windows). Swordeye ( ALX Theory , PC) - Mar & May 2026 The Milgram Experiment ( Theseus Games , PC) - Jan – Feb 2026 I Am Jesus Christ ( SimulaM , PC) - Jun 2025 Marathon ( Bungie , PC) - Apr – May 2025 3 Hit Blunders Bundle ( Late teur t’ gem , PC) - Sep – Oct 2024 Baldur’s Gate 3 ( Larian Studios , PC) - Oct 2020 – Aug 2023 Sea of Stars ( Sabotage Studio , PC) - Nov 2022 – Feb 2023 Spy Bros. (Pipi & Bibi’s DX) ( RAWRLAB Games , PC) - Jan 2023 Corgi Cove ( Recall Software , PC) - Jan 2023 The Anacrusis ( Stray Bombay , PC) - Oct – Dec 2021 New World ( Amazon Games , PC) - Jul 2020 – Aug 2021 Hello Neighbor ( Dynamic Pixels , PC) - Sep 2016 – Jul 2017 STEEP ( Ubisoft Annecy , PC) - Nov 2015 – Nov 2016 Battlerite ( Stunlock Studios , PC) - Sep 2016 Overwatch ( Blizzard Entertainment , PC) - Oct 2015 – May 2016 Paladins ( Hi-Rez Studios , PC) - Sep – Nov 2015 Never Alone (Kisima Ingitchuŋa) ( Upper One Games , PC) - Sep – Oct 2014 Star Swarm ( Oxide Games , PC) - Jan 2014 Divinity: Dragon Commander ( Larian Studios , PC) - Jun – Aug 2013 EverQuest Online Adventures ( Sony Online Entertainment , PlayStation 2) - Sep 2002 – Feb 2003 Shadowbane (Wolfpack Studios, PC) - Jan 2002 – Mar 2003 Game testing"
