"text": "← Back to Portfolio Sample course · Articulate Rise 360 Hands-Free Bag Checks How security officers inspect bags without touching them: safer for everyone, respectful of privacy, and effective against theft. I built this course for officers screening employees, vendors, and visitors at distribution and logistics sites. It explains why hands-free checks matter (safety, hygiene, and shrink), walks through the tools (flashlights, mirrors, dowel rods, wands, gloves, and trays) and a simple three-step process, and then covers what to do when a check turns something up: a weapon, a product without a pass, or nothing at all. A flowchart pulls the whole decision process together, and officers finish with a short quiz. Audience: Security officers who screen people entering and leaving client sites, and their supervisors. Open the course full screen Tip: the course has its own menu (top left). It works best in the full-screen version . Lessons Introduction to Hands-Free Bag Checks Tools and Equipment Step-by-Step Process Handling Issues Summary and Review Quiz Design features Narrated audio Safety training Process timelines Labeled graphics Flashcards Accordions Knowledge checks Final quiz ← Back to Portfolio"
