"text": "← Back to Portfolio Sample course · Articulate Rise 360 Use of Force: Legal, Ethical, and Practical Application for Philadelphia Security Officers Legal authority, core principles, the use-of-force continuum, de-escalation, and reporting, built to meet Philadelphia’s new training standard. I built this course to meet the minimum training standards Philadelphia set for private security officers (Bill No. 250646-A). It explains where an officer’s legal authority begins and ends, the principles of safety, necessity, and proportionality, how to move along the use-of-force continuum while de-escalating, and how to document an incident so the report protects everyone involved. Audience: Private security officers and supervisors working in Philadelphia. Open the course full screen Tip: the course has its own menu (top left). It works best in the full-screen version . Lessons Course Introduction: Purpose, Standards, and Learning Objectives Legal Authority & Boundaries of Private Security Core Principles of Use of Force Use of Force Continuum & Avoiding Escalation Reporting & Documentation Requirements Course Close: Key Takeaways and Final Quiz Design features Narrated audio Compliance training De-escalation Scenarios Knowledge checks Sorting activities Interactive tabs Accordions Final quiz ← Back to Portfolio"
